Z||000000||jlruiz67||06-13-2000||07:27 PM||||Hello <BR>Here goes a stupid question.<BR>There is a pcv valve that you can see once you open your trunk and it has easy access. I noticed that there is another hole on the other valve cover closest to the front of the car that has a pipe connected and it goes to the intake. Could someone tell me what is it and what is it for?<P>Thank you||||reg||4
Z||000001||btoth||06-13-2000||07:48 PM||||it just allows air to circulate into your engine (at least that's what i've been told) =)||||reg||1
Z||000002||RiceCooker||06-13-2000||07:58 PM||||Sometin like "btoth" said. It's the other side. I know this cause my bracket was bent on the far side and the steel pipe didn't match up to the engine - but it's fixed now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||06-13-2000||08:10 PM||||    The air inlet tube that you refered to is part of a recall. It moved the fresh air inlet from the intake side of the air cleaner to just in front of the throttle body. You might still have some remenant hosing on the fire wall that leads to the air intake just to the right of the air cleaner. Nothing to worry about. Someone on the forum actually has the recall notice, or at least a web address where you can view the actual notice.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||jlruiz67||06-13-2000||08:20 PM||||You guys are great. now for part two. what does it mean when you have oil leaking out of that air pipe and going into the intake?<BR>I think its probably re-build time but if any of you have and opinion I'll sure apreciate it. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fret Naught||06-14-2000||12:57 PM||||Sounds like Blow by to me, you need to do a compression test, to see what condition your valves/pistons are in. Could be just a valve job. Or it could be that I am all wet and don't know what I am talking about. I would suspect valves if it were mine||||reg||1
Z||000006||Linx||06-15-2000||10:46 PM||||yeppers...oil in that tube is blowby.  Time for a compression check.  Ordinarily, air is sucked <I>into</I> the engine thru that tube.  Engine gases are sucked <I>out</I> thru the PCV.  If youve got blowby, gasses will be ejected forcefully from <I>both</I> tubes.||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||06-16-2000||12:36 AM||||right - what they all said -- and by the way, there is no such thing as a "stupid question" on this forum - any of us will be happy to help you (we <I>do</I> get carried away sometimes tho, right Bam? Fret?.........and, welcome to the forum!!||||reg||1
